-- Children's Privacy Notice, rewritten: a short summary first, what a Kids profile collects in
-- groups, what we never collect, the AI features Kids profiles can use (only book text reaches
-- Anthropic), who sees it (Account → Family, the weekly report through Mailgun, support), how long
-- it's kept, withdrawing consent, and who to contact. src/data/legalPages.json has the same.
-- Only where the page is still the built-in text, so an editor's rewording is left as it is.

update public.legal_pages
set summary = $lw$For parents and guardians: what a Kids profile collects, why, who can see it, what we never collect, and how you stay in control. A Kids profile exists only with your consent, and you can see, download or delete everything it keeps.$lw$,
    sections = $lw$[{"heading": "In short", "paragraphs": ["A Kids profile lives inside your account. Only you, the account holder, can create one, and only after you consent.", "It keeps what it needs to work: a first name or nickname, an avatar and the child's reading. We never ask a child for an email address, full name, photo, location or any way to contact them.", "Its reading is private to your account. It isn't shown to other members, it isn't used for advertising, and it is never sold, rented or licensed.", "You can see it, download it, change its limits or delete it at any time from Account."]}, {"heading": "Your consent comes first", "paragraphs": ["Only the account holder, who must be 18 or older, can create a Kids profile or move a profile to Kids. You do it after reading this notice, and you confirm it with the account password.", "We keep a record of that consent: when it was given, how, and which version of this notice it was for.", "Moving the profile to another age rating, or deleting it, withdraws that consent, and we record that too."]}, {"heading": "What a Kids profile collects", "paragraphs": ["The profile: its first name or nickname, its avatar, its age rating, and any daily reading limit and weekly reading goal you set.", "Its reading: the books in its library, where it is in each book, its bookmarks, highlights and notes, its Up next queue, ratings, favourites and lists, the authors and narrators it follows, and its release reminders.", "Its time: how long it reads and listens each day, in total and for each book (shown on the book's page), the books it finishes, its reading goals and pace, and any reading plan it makes (the day it chose to finish by and where it was when the plan started).", "Its learning: the words it saves from the dictionary and when they're next due for review, its private reading journal, and its chapter quiz scores.", "Its family activity: the books it asks a grown-up for and your answers, and the household challenges it starts or joins, which the other profiles on your account can see.", "Badges are worked out on the device from this reading and are never stored. Books saved for offline reading stay on that device."]}, {"heading": "What we never collect", "paragraphs": ["We don't ask a child for their email address, full name, home address, school, phone number, photo, voice, location or any other way to contact them.", "A Kids profile can't write anything that other members see, so it can't share personal details with them.", "There's no advertising on LiteraryWorm, and we don't use analytics or advertising trackers."]}, {"heading": "What a Kids profile can't do", "paragraphs": ["Kids profiles see only books rated for children. A grown-up can say yes to a book above that rating when the child asks for it.", "They can't write public reading logs, join or start book clubs, follow other readers, share lists by link, upload or import books, search Google Books, ask the book's AI assistant or use Who's who.", "They can't make purchases or change account settings. A grown-up's password is needed to open Account or to allow extra time past a daily limit."]}, {"heading": "AI features", "paragraphs": ["A Kids profile can read AI-written book summaries, hear a recap of earlier chapters (Previously…) and take chapter quizzes. These are written by Claude, made by Anthropic.", "We send Anthropic only the book's details or its own text and which chapter it's about, never the child's name, answers, scores or anything else about them. The summaries, recaps and quizzes are kept and shared with every reader of that book, so they say nothing about who asked."]}, {"heading": "Who sees it", "paragraphs": ["You do: Account → Family shows each Kids profile's last 7 days, its weekly goal, its book requests and its quiz scores.", "If you turn on the weekly Kids reading report, we email last week's reading to your account's email address. Mailgun sends it for us. It's off until you turn it on.", "Our hosting providers, Supabase and Vercel, store and serve it only to run LiteraryWorm for you.", "Our support team can see how many profiles an account has, but not a profile's name, library, reading, notes or journal."]}, {"heading": "How long we keep it", "paragraphs": ["We keep a Kids profile's information for as long as the profile exists.", "Deleting the profile, or your whole account, deletes everything it collected from our database straight away. Copies in our providers' backups are removed when those backups expire."]}, {"heading": "Your choices as a parent", "paragraphs": ["From Account you can see the profile's activity, download a copy of your data, change its daily limit, weekly goal and age rating, and answer its book requests.", "You can add a PIN to the other profiles so a child can't open them.", "You can stop us collecting anything more at any time by deleting the profile, which deletes everything it collected. Moving it to another age rating also ends the Kids protections, but keeps its reading under its new rating."]}, {"heading": "Questions", "paragraphs": ["If you have a question about your child's information, or think a child is using LiteraryWorm without a parent's consent, email usprivacy@literaryworm.com. We'll answer, and we'll delete information collected without consent.", "The Privacy Policy explains how we handle everyone's information, including your rights where you live."]}]$lw$::jsonb,
    updated_at = now()
where slug = $lw$childrens-privacy$lw$
  and sections = $lw$[{"heading": "Your consent comes first", "paragraphs": ["Only the account holder, who must be 18 or older, can create a Kids profile or move a profile to Kids, and only after reading this notice and confirming with the account password. We keep a record of that consent: when it was given, how, and which version of this notice it was for."]}, {"heading": "What a Kids profile collects", "paragraphs": ["The profile's first name or nickname and avatar, its age rating and any daily reading limit and weekly reading goal you set, and its reading: the books in its library, where it is in each book, bookmarks, highlights and notes, the words it saves from the dictionary, its private reading journal, the books it asks a grown-up for and your answers (which you give and can see in Account), its chapter quiz scores (which you can see in Account), its Up next queue and reading pace, ratings, favourites and lists, the authors and narrators it follows, release reminders, reading time and goals. The time it spends with each book, day by day, is kept too, to show it on the book's page. If it makes a reading plan, we keep the day it chose to finish the book by and where it was when the plan started.", "We don't ask a child for their email, full name, address, photo, location or any other contact details."]}, {"heading": "What a Kids profile can't do", "paragraphs": ["Kids profiles see only books rated for children. They can't write public reading logs, join or start book clubs, share lists by link, upload books, ask the book's AI assistant, make purchases or change account settings. A grown-up's password is needed to open Account or to allow extra time past a daily limit."]}, {"heading": "Who sees it", "paragraphs": ["A Kids profile's reading is private to your account. It isn't shown to other members, isn't used for advertising, and is never sold, rented or licensed. Our hosting providers (Supabase and Vercel) store it only to run LiteraryWorm for you."]}, {"heading": "Your choices as a parent", "paragraphs": ["From Account you can see and download the profile's data, change its limits, add a PIN to other profiles so a child can't open them, move the profile to another age rating, or delete it, which deletes everything it collected. You can withdraw consent at any time by deleting the profile."]}]$lw$::jsonb;
